  "term": "nAchR",
  "definition": "nAchR refers to the nicotinic acetylcholine receptor, a transmembrane protein complex that opens a cation channel when acetylcholine or nicotine binds to it. These receptors are found in many tissues and help support neurotransmission, muscle contraction, and inflammatory processes.",
